    <briefdescription>
<para>Front-end-side description of a monomial ordering as a list of <computeroutput>mon_part</computeroutput> blocks. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><computeroutput><ref refid="struct_monomial_ordering_af01636236f198af374d761786461de27_1af01636236f198af374d761786461de27" kindref="member">_hash</ref></computeroutput> caches the front-end hash so order objects can be compared and deduplicated cheaply; <computeroutput><ref refid="struct_monomial_ordering_a4d4b8bd4a33482af83efaca798a33519_1a4d4b8bd4a33482af83efaca798a33519" kindref="member">len</ref></computeroutput> is the number of blocks; <computeroutput><ref refid="struct_monomial_ordering_a50917e95eea25ef79478905ec6d244ca_1a50917e95eea25ef79478905ec6d244ca" kindref="member">array</ref>[1]</computeroutput> is a C99 flexible-array tail holding the <computeroutput><ref refid="struct_monomial_ordering_a4d4b8bd4a33482af83efaca798a33519_1a4d4b8bd4a33482af83efaca798a33519" kindref="member">len</ref></computeroutput> ordered blocks (<computeroutput>Lex</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>GRevLex</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>Weights</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>Position</computeroutput>, ...). Built by the <computeroutput><ref refid="class_monomial_orderings" kindref="compound">MonomialOrderings</ref>::*</computeroutput> factories (<computeroutput><ref refid="monordering_8hpp" kindref="compound">monordering.hpp</ref></computeroutput>) and compiled into the engine-side <computeroutput><ref refid="struct_monomial_order__rec" kindref="compound">MonomialOrder_rec</ref></computeroutput> (<computeroutput><ref refid="imonorder_8hpp" kindref="compound">imonorder.hpp</ref></computeroutput>) via <computeroutput><ref refid="imonorder_8cpp_a569a1b1cac1332509ad69d7153a69256_1a569a1b1cac1332509ad69d7153a69256" kindref="member">monomialOrderMake</ref></computeroutput>. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
